.TH yes 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
yes \- print a string over and over
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yes
[\fIstring\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B yes
writes
.I string
followed by a newline, endlessly, until the write fails \- which is what
happens when the program it is feeding exits.  With no argument it
writes
.BR y .
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH NOTES
Only the first argument is used; the rest are ignored.
.PP
Run on a terminal by mistake it will fill the screen until you interrupt
it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sh (1)
